2. 4C fast charge, plated=false (stage3): anode_potential_v ≥ 0 V throughout 4C charge at 45°C. Levers: N/P ratio (thicker negative), particle size (smaller → less concentration polarization — T1 measured +14.6 contribution), electrolyte transport (σ, t⁺, D), porosity. 45°C helps (faster transport). Trade-off: thicker negative adds mass → ED down.
3. SEI ≤ 550 nm after 100 cycles at 45°C (stage2): SEI growth accelerates with temperature. Levers: SEI kinetic rate constant (coating — electrode modification), SEI reaction exchange current density. Baseline measurement first. Reference magnitude: Chen2020-set SEI kinetics ×0.1 → 449→385 nm at RT (skill's measured signal-scale reference).
