yte oxidative decomposition (high voltage) | Electrolyte HOMO above cathode window | **No molecular-funnel HOMO value produced** (start_stage = 3; real_compute = false; endorse skipped) — detectability: N/A (not simulated) | Medium | Low (qualitative: NMC811/carbonate is an established system; 4.2 V cut-off per parameter set) | Voltage window unchanged (2.5–4.2 V); true DFT/MD endorsement listed as follow-up in DVPR N/A section |\n| 5 | Insufficient capacity | Electrode loading too low | 1C capacity 5.0065 Ah vs nominal 5.0 Ah (PASS) — signal: `capacity_ah` | Medium | Low | Nominal loading preserved (positive untouched; negative reverted to baseline 85.2 µm) |\n| 6 | 4C charge thermal overshoot | High-rate heat generation vs cooling capacity | 4C @45 °C: T_max 325.54 K vs 573 K red line — signal: `T_max_K` | High | Low | h = 100 W/m²/K liquid cooling; +7.39 K rise only |\n| 7 | Thermal-runaway prediction blow-up (virtual ODE artifact) | Arrhenius ODE runaway branch produces unphysical post-trigger temperatures (10⁴–10⁹ K in triggered runs) | Annotated in every evaluate entry; only the `triggered` boolean is treated as meaningful | — | — | Honesty annotation; not a design risk (see note) |\n\n## Conclusion\n\nHighest-risk items: #1 plating (High severity — mitigated to Low occurrence by design, margin +15.3 mV) and #2 thermal runaway (High severity — mitigated to Low occurrence but **conditional on the cooling system being present**; occurrence High if cooling is omitted). #3 SEI margin is the thinnest quantitative margin (+39.5 nm / 7.2%) and is flagged for the physical-prototype follow-up (e.g., electrolyte-additive formulation beyond this parameter set). Mitigation measures above are implemented in the final R5 design (params_r5_slim.json). Complete FMEA including process/supplier failure modes: **N/A (beyond pure simulation boundary)**. Item 7 is an artifact annotation, not a failure mode of the design.\n"}
